            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked why these sentences are not mandatory, noting the jury had only two choices, death or life without parole."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned whether the judge knew he could exercise discretion given the lack of prior history."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked how a discretionary sentencing scheme satisfies the substantive right recognized in Miller and Montgomery."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg followed up on the government\u2019s change in position regarding whether juveniles sentenced to life without parole must be resentenced after Miller and Montgomery."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether judges who consider age under post\u2011Jones statutes are presumed to follow Miller and Montgomery."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked whether the statutes set out the factors required by Miller and Montgomery and require courts to evaluate them."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked whether competent defense counsel would argue the youth factor in a discretionary regime where life without parole is possible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, justice Gorsuch raised the question of whether a Sixth Amendment right requires a jury, rather than a judge, to find incorrigibility before imposing life without parole."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
              "start": 66
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether a juvenile who demonstrates rehabilitation must be released."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "71b68fec51fe737c782f16ec87c00d83633dae3f433699380ac80f5028843b98",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-71b68fec51fe-0003-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 69,
              "start": 69
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor inquired about a case where counsel raised the youth argument and the judge claimed no power to consider it."
      }
    ],
